7
00:00:42.576 --> 00:00:43.908
(WHIRRING)

8
00:00:56.924 --> 00:00:58.153
(GROANING)

9
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.160
(MAN PANTING)

10
00:01:08.135 --> 00:01:11.435
Oh. my God. Oh. my God.

11
00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.605
MAN: She's still breathing.
Call 911. Hurry up. Call 911.

12
00:01:37.898 --> 00:01:39.025
Kiss me.

13
00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:44.030
Hello. Yeah. I was
in a car accident

14
00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:47.541
and a woman got hit.
She's hurt really bad.

15
00:01:50.077 --> 00:01:51.670
She's just lying on the ground.

16
00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.520
She's still breathing.

17
00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:18.128
(INDISTINCT TALKING
ON POLICE RADIO)

18
00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.275
Driver of the car is Leroy Kent.

19
00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.586
Says he's driving
home from work.

20
00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.288
drives onto the bridge.
sees the victim running.

21
00:02:25.312 --> 00:02:26.522
she runs right
in front of his car.

22
00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.572
Says it happened so
fast. couldn't do anything.

23
00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:29.742
Get an ID on the vic?

24
00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.728
No wallet. no purse. Looks
like she just got out of bed.

25
00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:33.152
Did Mr. Kent have
anything to drink?

26
00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.831
He's had a couple.
but he's under the limit.

27
00:02:34.855 --> 00:02:36.653
Any witnesses? Well.

28
00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.867
driver said there
was one other guy.

29
00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.360
Told him to call 911.
but he didn't stick around.

30
00:02:40.427 --> 00:02:42.362
We got guys out
doing a canvass now.

31
00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:44.330
Mr. Kent. Yes.

32
00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:46.196
How are you feeling?

33
00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.393
Is she dead?

34
00:02:48.435 --> 00:02:49.459
Yeah.

35
00:02:49.803 --> 00:02:51.362
At first I thought
she might be okay.

36
00:02:51.438 --> 00:02:53.236
I mean. the guy said
she was still breathing.

37
00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.400
Is this the guy who
told you to call 911?

38
00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.707
Yes. I ran over there
as soon as it happened

39
00:02:59.046 --> 00:03:00.139
and he just walked up.

40
00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.340
Where'd he go?

41
00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:06.616
I don't know. I called 911. I
looked back. he was gone.

42
00:03:07.154 --> 00:03:08.383
Any idea what he looked like?

43
00:03:08.455 --> 00:03:09.855
Not really. no.

44
00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:15.091
I was pretty shook up. I
was paying attention to her.

45
00:03:17.097 --> 00:03:19.157
We're done. if you
guys want to take a look.

46
00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.325
Yeah.

47
00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.794
Thank you. Mr. Kent.

48
00:03:27.841 --> 00:03:30.367
Barefoot. ready for bed.
but still wearing makeup.

49
00:03:30.644 --> 00:03:32.306
Maybe she wasn't alone.

50
00:03:33.447 --> 00:03:34.745
We've got some glass here.

51
00:03:34.815 --> 00:03:36.759
Windshield didn't shatter
and headlights are still intact.

52
00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.094
This didn't come
from the accident.

53
00:03:38.118 --> 00:03:39.662
There's no cuts or
abrasions on her feet.

54
00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.087
The guy said she was running.
She couldn't have run too far.

55
00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:43.981
I wonder where
she was running to.

56
00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.923
Or what she was running from.

57
00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.460
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

58
00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.898
(IN FRENCH)

59
00:04:25.966 --> 00:04:27.332
I'll call when it's finished.

60
00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.168
HARPER: Notice
the iris is fully dilated.

61
00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.332
filling the eye completely.

62
00:05:07.574 --> 00:05:09.174
Looks like a shark's
eye. Is that normal?

63
00:05:09.209 --> 00:05:10.889
Well. there's usually
dilation after death.

64
00:05:10.944 --> 00:05:12.744
but I've never seen
anything like this before.

65
00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.439
You get a tox report?

66
00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.608
Preliminary says she
had a few drinks. not a lot.

67
00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.549
Alcohol was .06.

68
00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:19.711
What about drugs?

69
00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:21.414
So far none of
the usual suspects.

70
00:05:21.488 --> 00:05:23.432
Finding the unusual is
going to take a little more time.

71
00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:24.947
Any sign of sexual assault?

72
00:05:25.559 --> 00:05:27.119
No. But there was
something interesting.

73
00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.061
No crush on the lungs.

74
00:05:29.129 --> 00:05:30.290
What does that mean?

75
00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:33.561
She was asphyxiated. but it
wasn't a result of the accident.

76
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.929
Someone suffocated her
after she was hit by the car?

77
00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:38.802
So we got a homicide?

78
00:05:38.872 --> 00:05:40.932
These contusions around
her nose and mouth.

79
00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.600
looks like somebody
pinched off her air.

80
00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:43.974
HANK: I got a hit on her prints.

81
00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:46.669
The victim's name
was Faith Collins. 33.

82
00:05:47.314 --> 00:05:49.554
Busted for a DUI a few months
ago. License was suspended.

83
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:50.846
Get an address?

84
00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.517
About a mile away
from where she got hit.

85
00:05:52.586 --> 00:05:53.763
We knew she didn't run very far.

86
00:05:53.787 --> 00:05:55.653
so it makes sense
that she lived close by.

87
00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:56.999
Well. maybe she was
running from home.

88
00:05:57.023 --> 00:06:00.289
I think maybe she was running
from her husband. Roy Collins.

89
00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.760
Got a record for spousal abuse.

90
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.596
(WHIRRING)

91
00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.325
You Roy Collins?

92
00:06:14.074 --> 00:06:16.634
What'd she tell you?
She saying I hit her?

93
00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.521
She didn't say anything.
Well. that's different.

94
00:06:18.545 --> 00:06:20.639
She usually complains
about everything I do.

95
00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:23.582
Well. she's not going to
be complaining anymore.

96
00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.151
We found your
wife's body last night.

97
00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:29.014
What? Your wife's been murdered.

98
00:06:29.089 --> 00:06:30.421
Oh. no.

99
00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:33.725
I know this is difficult. but we need
to know the last time you saw her.

100
00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:37.322
(STUTTERING) Last night.

101
00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.461
What happened?

102
00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:44.235
I came home. and I was hungry.

103
00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.449
Faith wouldn't get off
the computer. like always.

104
00:06:46.473 --> 00:06:48.533
She's got to connect
with her 322 friends.

105
00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:51.635
I mean. who the
hell's got 322 friends?

106
00:06:52.279 --> 00:06:54.339
I mean. I'm hungry.
I've been working all day.

107
00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.905
So you argued? Yeah.

108
00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.243
And she walked
out. you know. mad.

109
00:06:58.318 --> 00:07:00.514
I didn't mean anything I said.

110
00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:02.031
Well. did she tell you
where she was going?

111
00:07:02.055 --> 00:07:03.079
No. You go after her?

112
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.483
No. NICK: About what
time did she leave?

113
00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:08.695
I don't know. 10:00
or something like that.

114
00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.242
So she left. you stayed
home. That's your story?

115
00:07:11.298 --> 00:07:12.732
It's the truth.

116
00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:14.495
Anybody see you?
You talk to anybody?

117
00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.058
No.

118
00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.930
I was waiting for
her to come back.

119
00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:21.866
She always comes back.

120
00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.538
You guys think I did
something to her?

121
00:07:28.949 --> 00:07:30.781
You think I'd kill
my wife? Did you?

122
00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:33.379
Want to do yourself a favor?

123
00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.697
Why don't you come
downtown with us.

124
00:07:34.721 --> 00:07:37.816
we'll put you in a
lineup. What do you say?

125
00:07:37.891 --> 00:07:40.486
You want me for a
lineup? Arrest me.

126
00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:43.560
But you don't got anything
on me. 'cause I didn't do it.

127
00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.259
Where is she?

128
00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.300
Her body's in the morgue.

129
00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:52.228
When do I get her?

130
00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.630
Somebody will contact you.

131
00:07:59.746 --> 00:08:00.805
RENARD: What do you got?

132
00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:01.958
NICK: Well. according
to her credit card.

133
00:08:01.982 --> 00:08:04.884
Faith had a couple drinks at a bar
called the Blue Moon at around 10:30.

134
00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:06.920
Bartender said she
talked up a couple locals.

135
00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:08.631
but she left alone.
She didn't have her car.

136
00:08:08.655 --> 00:08:09.748
Her license is suspended.

137
00:08:09.823 --> 00:08:11.734
We're checking with cab companies
now to see who picked her up.

138
00:08:11.758 --> 00:08:14.193
Called to the house four
times for domestic disturbance.

139
00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.980
The husband's been
arrested twice for abuse.

140
00:08:16.029 --> 00:08:18.274
I mean. it sounds like a battered
wife who couldn't break the cycle.

141
00:08:18.298 --> 00:08:19.508
You sure the
husband's not covering?

142
00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.660
Could be. He admits
to arguing with her.

143
00:08:21.735 --> 00:08:23.636
Any chance she talked
to a family member

144
00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:24.847
about her problems last night?

145
00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.271
No calls on her cell after 9:00.

146
00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:30.034
What about her 322 friends. Maybe
she reached out to one of them.

147
00:08:31.745 --> 00:08:34.271
Hey. check it. She
posted last night.

148
00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:36.539
Looks like a park.

149
00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:38.642
Or a private garden.
What time did she send it?

150
00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:41.153
11:37. Now if this was
taken from her cell phone.

151
00:08:41.221 --> 00:08:45.158
the GPS coordinates should
be embedded in the file. right?

152
00:08:45.225 --> 00:08:47.490
1516 Longacre Road.

153
00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.994
Map it.

154
00:08:52.599 --> 00:08:55.501
That's right here.

155
00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:57.098
HANK: Right near the bridge.

156
00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.570
NICK: Definitely
running distance.

157
00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.765
Click "location."

158
00:09:02.876 --> 00:09:04.708
"The Bramble Haus.
Bed and Breakfast."

159
00:09:05.078 --> 00:09:06.078
You know it?

160
00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.371
When do I have time
for a bed or breakfast?

161
00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:10.593
Let's check with
the cab companies.

162
00:09:10.617 --> 00:09:14.179
see if they made any drop-offs
at a B&B you don't have time for.

163
00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:29.835
Not bad. You should make
time for a place like this.

164
00:09:29.903 --> 00:09:32.702
Check out this '67 MGB Roadster.

165
00:09:32.772 --> 00:09:34.536
You ready for a
little bit of trivia?

166
00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:36.303
Royal blue and chrome bumpers.

167
00:09:36.376 --> 00:09:38.368
Collectors call that
model right there

168
00:09:38.445 --> 00:09:40.346
"the most desirable
MG ever made."

169
00:09:41.281 --> 00:09:42.749
Impressed? Mildly.

170
00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:47.163
BILLY: <i>Of course.
Yes. I remember her.</i>

171
00:09:47.187 --> 00:09:49.713
She came in. I'd
say. it was after 11:00.

172
00:09:49.789 --> 00:09:52.258
I was in the kitchen pulling
up some biscuits for breakfast

173
00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:54.556
and I heard the bell ring.
so I went and got the door.

174
00:09:54.627 --> 00:09:57.119
Oh! Excuse me a minute.

175
00:09:57.197 --> 00:09:58.529
I've got your bill right here.

176
00:09:58.598 --> 00:09:59.708
I hope everything
was to your liking.

177
00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:02.998
Oh. Billy. we just love
this place. It's so magical.

178
00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:04.093
Thank you. Thank you.

179
00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.247
MAN: Yeah. we'll see
you on our anniversary.

180
00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:07.399
BILLY: I look forward
to it. And tell your friends.

181
00:10:07.474 --> 00:10:08.942
WOMAN: Five stars on Yelp.

182
00:10:09.576 --> 00:10:12.205
And. you two. you guys
are going to love this place.

183
00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:17.550
Newlyweds. They're
a third of my business.

184
00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:18.761
So. I'm sorry. where were we?

185
00:10:18.785 --> 00:10:19.844
The girl.

186
00:10:19.919 --> 00:10:21.512
Of course. right. yes. Um...

187
00:10:21.588 --> 00:10:23.352
I showed her a
room and the garden.

188
00:10:23.423 --> 00:10:24.721
But she didn't stay?

189
00:10:24.791 --> 00:10:26.350
No. she didn't
have a bag with her.

190
00:10:26.426 --> 00:10:27.621
I'm sorry is there a problem?

191
00:10:27.694 --> 00:10:29.720
A cab dropped her off
and didn't pick her up.

192
00:10:29.796 --> 00:10:31.458
Can you explain that?
I really don't know.

193
00:10:31.531 --> 00:10:33.742
I mean. if they don't want
to stay. I can't force them to.

194
00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:35.325
You know. to tell you the truth.

195
00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:38.098
she seemed a little bit
concerned or troubled.

196
00:10:38.171 --> 00:10:39.615
And it's not really my
place to get involved

197
00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:40.919
in guests' personal lives. so...

198
00:10:41.508 --> 00:10:42.567
Can we see the garden?

199
00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:44.577
Of course. yes. Oh...

200
00:10:44.644 --> 00:10:47.443
But I warn you. you
might want to stay.

201
00:10:47.514 --> 00:10:48.514
(LAUGHS)

202
00:10:49.549 --> 00:10:50.573
Oh! Excuse me.

203
00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:53.783
No problem.

204
00:11:04.931 --> 00:11:06.422
Hey.

205
00:11:12.405 --> 00:11:15.898
Yeah. this is the place. She
came here and then what?

206
00:11:16.109 --> 00:11:20.046
I showed her these amber
roses that bloom only in Portland.

207
00:11:20.113 --> 00:11:25.313
and my flowering wisteria.
And of course. the agapanthus.

208
00:11:25.385 --> 00:11:27.251
but don't get me
started on those.

209
00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:29.031
And then she said she
wanted to sit for a moment

210
00:11:29.055 --> 00:11:30.956
and gather her thoughts.
so I said that this...

211
00:11:31.024 --> 00:11:33.050
Be careful where you
step! That's... (SQUISHING)

212
00:11:34.794 --> 00:11:36.956
Sorry. I didn't mean to do that.

213
00:12:02.388 --> 00:12:05.153
The toad is an
endangered species.

214
00:12:05.225 --> 00:12:07.421
It's the first sign of our
extinction when toads die.

215
00:12:07.627 --> 00:12:09.459
I'm sorry. I didn't see it.

216
00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.264
Well. if you can
think of anything else.

217
00:12:14.334 --> 00:12:16.803
Of course. Yes. I'll
contact you immediately.

218
00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.614
Would you like me
to show you out?

219
00:12:18.638 --> 00:12:19.970
No. We're good.

220
00:12:21.641 --> 00:12:22.641
Hey.

221
00:12:28.314 --> 00:12:29.441
Have a good day.

222
00:12:44.163 --> 00:12:45.756
That's all I got. Jim.

223
00:12:45.832 --> 00:12:48.131
Let me know if you
need anything else. yeah?

224
00:12:54.707 --> 00:12:55.800
Can I help you?

225
00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:58.777
Yes. I'm looking into the
death of a friend of mine.

226
00:12:58.845 --> 00:13:01.110
He was shot by one
of your detectives.

227
00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.773
Are you a lawyer? No.

228
00:13:02.849 --> 00:13:04.010
Just a friend of the family.

229
00:13:04.384 --> 00:13:06.376
Here's the newspaper
article. I brought it along

230
00:13:06.452 --> 00:13:07.972
so you'd know what
I was talking about.

231
00:13:08.221 --> 00:13:09.780
Take a seat. please.

232
00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:14.886
WU: He wants to talk to
the officer who shot his friend.

233
00:13:15.762 --> 00:13:16.991
What did you tell him?

234
00:13:17.063 --> 00:13:19.541
I told him we don't give out
that information. Sir. he's waiting.

235
00:13:19.565 --> 00:13:20.885
How do you want
me to handle this?

236
00:13:21.334 --> 00:13:22.711
Tell him the
detective's not available.

237
00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:25.261
that someone from the
department will get back to him.

238
00:13:25.338 --> 00:13:26.601
Yes. sir.

239
00:13:26.673 --> 00:13:28.473
Make sure to get his
name. number and address.

240
00:13:29.042 --> 00:13:30.642
Do a background check
and get back to me.

241
00:13:38.151 --> 00:13:39.551
(INAUDIBLE)

242
00:13:42.021 --> 00:13:44.733
The cab picked her up from the bar.
but why did she go to the Bramble Haus?

243
00:13:44.757 --> 00:13:46.535
She was probably just
looking for a place to stay

244
00:13:46.559 --> 00:13:48.289
so she wouldn't
have to go back home.

245
00:13:48.361 --> 00:13:49.672
Cab driver could
have recommended it.

246
00:13:49.696 --> 00:13:50.939
What does it matter.
she didn't stay.

247
00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:52.007
That's what we need to find out.

248
00:13:52.031 --> 00:13:53.431
She went there.
but she didn't stay.

249
00:13:53.466 --> 00:13:54.743
And she didn't
call for another cab.

250
