499
00:33:25.337 --> 00:33:26.635
No way.

500
00:33:27.305 --> 00:33:30.207
Dude. I can't be around
that guy. He's way too potent.

501
00:33:30.675 --> 00:33:32.143
I almost bought him a drink.

502
00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:34.111
No. I need you
to go back inside.

503
00:33:34.179 --> 00:33:35.619
I need to know
what he's going to do.

504
00:33:35.647 --> 00:33:36.740
He's hitting on a girl.

505
00:33:36.815 --> 00:33:39.546
She's buying the
full toad. you know?

506
00:33:39.918 --> 00:33:41.596
He gave her his card. What
more do you need to know?

507
00:33:41.620 --> 00:33:43.020
What? What. now you're mad?

508
00:33:43.088 --> 00:33:44.317
He's coming out.

509
00:33:50.695 --> 00:33:52.220
(WHISPERING) You
want me to track him?

510
00:33:52.297 --> 00:33:53.629
No. You're done.

511
00:33:53.698 --> 00:33:55.064
You did good. Thank you.

512
00:33:56.835 --> 00:33:58.064
You can go home now.

513
00:34:01.139 --> 00:34:03.040
I don't want to go home now.

514
00:34:17.355 --> 00:34:18.933
You know if you like
gardens. I happen to...

515
00:34:18.957 --> 00:34:20.448
Piss off. Okay.

516
00:34:21.693 --> 00:34:23.355
One more. Please.

517
00:34:31.469 --> 00:34:33.836
Hank. come on. where
the hell are you. man?

518
00:34:33.905 --> 00:34:35.669
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

519
00:34:39.878 --> 00:34:41.779
Pick up the damn phone!
He's on his way home.

520
00:35:18.116 --> 00:35:19.277
OFFICER: <i>Portland Police.</i>

521
00:35:19.351 --> 00:35:20.717
Yeah. it's Detective Burkhardt.

522
00:35:20.785 --> 00:35:22.413
I need a 20 on
Detective Griffin.

523
00:35:22.487 --> 00:35:23.853
Track his cell.

524
00:35:23.922 --> 00:35:24.946
<i>Tracking now.</i>

525
00:35:25.023 --> 00:35:26.184
Yeah. I'll stay on the line.

526
00:35:26.257 --> 00:35:27.850
(AIR HISSING)

527
00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:36.593
(HISSING STOPS)

528
00:35:52.684 --> 00:35:53.708
<i>Still tracking.</i>

529
00:35:53.785 --> 00:35:55.425
All right. call me back
when you find him.

530
00:36:03.294 --> 00:36:04.626
That was fast.

531
00:36:04.696 --> 00:36:06.426
Why wait? I'm ready.

532
00:36:06.631 --> 00:36:08.827
Fantastic. I'll show you a room.

533
00:36:08.900 --> 00:36:10.100
I promise you won't regret it.

534
00:36:10.602 --> 00:36:12.264
I really want to
see your garden.

535
00:36:13.338 --> 00:36:17.469
It's late. But I think I have one
more tour left in me. Come on.

536
00:36:23.415 --> 00:36:24.415
Remember me?

537
00:36:24.949 --> 00:36:26.577
Of course. yes.
You're the detective.

538
00:36:26.985 --> 00:36:28.214
What can I do for you?

539
00:36:28.353 --> 00:36:29.480
I need to talk to her.

540
00:36:29.554 --> 00:36:30.647
Me?

541
00:36:30.789 --> 00:36:32.519
Would you mind stepping outside?

542
00:36:32.590 --> 00:36:34.320
I just need to ask
you a few questions.

543
00:36:34.993 --> 00:36:37.019
Am I in trouble?
What's this all about?

544
00:36:37.095 --> 00:36:38.688
Just come outside. please.

545
00:36:39.631 --> 00:36:40.758
I'm sure it'll be fine.

546
00:36:40.899 --> 00:36:42.060
Why don't you go with him

547
00:36:42.133 --> 00:36:44.227
and I'll be here
when you get back.

548
00:36:45.003 --> 00:36:46.471
Okay. Okay?

549
00:36:54.879 --> 00:36:56.624
I wish you'd just tell
me what this is all about.

550
00:36:56.648 --> 00:36:58.742
You walked into the middle
of a police investigation.

551
00:36:58.817 --> 00:36:59.841
(CELL PHONE RINGS)

552
00:36:59.918 --> 00:37:02.854
I need you to leave
the premises. Now!

553
00:37:04.456 --> 00:37:05.515
Yeah?

554
00:37:05.590 --> 00:37:07.388
OFFICER: <i>We've got a
20 on Detective Griffin.</i>

555
00:37:07.459 --> 00:37:09.621
<i>We've identified the
location as the Bramble Haus.</i>

556
00:37:09.694 --> 00:37:11.754
<i>Bed and Breakfast
on Longacre Road.</i>

557
00:37:11.830 --> 00:37:12.854
Thanks.

558
00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:37.084
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

559
00:37:46.698 --> 00:37:47.698
Hank?

560
00:37:51.336 --> 00:37:52.531
Hank!

561
00:38:02.180 --> 00:38:03.671
(WOMAN MOANS)

562
00:38:05.450 --> 00:38:06.577
Where are you?

563
00:38:06.651 --> 00:38:07.744
HANK: Nick.

564
00:38:10.455 --> 00:38:11.548
What happened?

565
00:38:11.623 --> 00:38:14.388
I don't know. man.
It's some kind of gas.

566
00:38:14.459 --> 00:38:15.654
Look here.

567
00:38:18.830 --> 00:38:19.830
Are they real?

568
00:38:22.433 --> 00:38:23.924
(AIR HISSING)

569
00:38:26.805 --> 00:38:28.467
He's got some kind
of gas coming in here.

570
00:38:28.873 --> 00:38:30.068
Got to get them out of here.

571
00:38:30.141 --> 00:38:31.786
Yeah. but we have to
shut that gas off first.

572
00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:33.176
We'll come back for them.

573
00:38:43.288 --> 00:38:44.288
Oh!

574
00:38:45.356 --> 00:38:46.585
I couldn't stay away.

575
00:38:47.192 --> 00:38:48.353
Lucky me.

576
00:38:48.426 --> 00:38:49.621
You leaving?

577
00:38:49.994 --> 00:38:51.223
Yes. it's such a lovely night.

578
00:38:51.296 --> 00:38:52.730
I thought that I
would take a drive.

579
00:38:52.797 --> 00:38:54.789
I was hoping I could stay.

580
00:38:54.866 --> 00:38:56.143
Well. why don't you come with me

581
00:38:56.167 --> 00:38:57.601
and we can talk about it. okay?

582
00:38:57.669 --> 00:38:59.194
Okay.

583
00:39:06.177 --> 00:39:07.177
(SCREAMS)

584
00:39:07.545 --> 00:39:08.545
Did you see that?

585
00:39:08.613 --> 00:39:10.775
What are you talking
about? Stand back.

586
00:39:11.349 --> 00:39:13.409
No. the gas is going to blow.

587
00:39:13.484 --> 00:39:15.362
We got to find something
to break this door open.

588
00:39:15.386 --> 00:39:17.116
No time. Just us.

589
00:39:18.990 --> 00:39:20.049
Let's do it.

590
00:39:20.124 --> 00:39:22.116
One. two. three!

591
00:39:22.327 --> 00:39:23.659
(BOTH GRUNTING)

592
00:39:24.462 --> 00:39:27.830
Again. One. two. three.

593
00:39:31.970 --> 00:39:33.529
(HISSING STOPS)

594
00:39:40.144 --> 00:39:41.737
(INDISTINCT)

595
00:39:44.949 --> 00:39:47.441
You're going to be
all right now. It's over.

596
00:39:48.620 --> 00:39:51.818
House is clean. car is
gone. He's in the wind.

597
00:39:52.523 --> 00:39:54.068
God. I'd hate to lose
this son of a bitch.

598
00:39:54.092 --> 00:39:55.685
No more than I do.

599
00:40:10.575 --> 00:40:12.601
Let it be my birthday.

600
00:40:20.451 --> 00:40:22.386
You didn't get that
grease spot for nothing.

601
00:40:37.368 --> 00:40:38.734
Here you go.

602
00:40:39.804 --> 00:40:40.804
Thanks.

603
00:40:40.905 --> 00:40:42.567
We should really get going soon.

604
00:40:43.274 --> 00:40:45.106
I can't believe I'm doing this.

605
00:40:45.176 --> 00:40:47.577
I've never done
anything like this before.

606
00:40:47.779 --> 00:40:49.270
Am I crazy?

607
00:40:49.347 --> 00:40:51.145
Maybe I'm crazy to take you.

608
00:40:54.919 --> 00:40:56.353
Are we leaving now?

609
00:40:56.421 --> 00:40:57.514
Stop! Police!

610
00:40:57.588 --> 00:40:58.783
Billy!

611
00:40:59.357 --> 00:41:00.723
Police! Out of the way!

612
00:41:09.033 --> 00:41:11.059
Billy Capra. stay where you are!

613
00:41:20.712 --> 00:41:22.340
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

614
00:41:23.781 --> 00:41:24.781
Get down!

615
00:41:44.635 --> 00:41:46.467
(TIRES SCREECHING) (GROANING)

616
00:41:55.713 --> 00:41:57.079
HANK: This is one sick dude.

617
00:41:57.148 --> 00:41:59.413
NICK: We sent his DNA to
Tucson. Des Moines and Detroit

618
00:41:59.484 --> 00:42:00.975
and I'm betting
it's the same guy.

619
00:42:01.052 --> 00:42:02.129
Well. at least
he's off the streets.

620
00:42:02.153 --> 00:42:03.644
and out of the hotel business.

621
00:42:03.721 --> 00:42:06.247
I can't believe any of these
women want to be near this guy.

622
00:42:06.324 --> 00:42:08.850
You know what? I'm
betting it's the toads.

623
00:42:08.926 --> 00:42:10.724
Yeah. right. toads.

624
00:42:10.795 --> 00:42:12.764
(SCOFFS) If only
it was that easy.

625
00:42:12.830 --> 00:42:14.765
Maybe I'll get me some toads.

626
00:42:20.004 --> 00:42:23.566
See how he likes being in
a cage for the rest of his life.

626
00:42:24.305 --> 00:43:24.167
-== [ www.OpenSubtitles.org ] ==-
